+## [0.44.1-fork.1] - 2026-07-31
+
+Selective P0/P1 sync on the current stable upstream v0.44.1 base, plus the
+upstream multiline and safe-consumer pipeline rewrite branches.
+
+### Added
+- Rewrites independent commands in multiline Bash blocks while preserving
+  quoted multiline strings and unsafe cross-line constructs.
+- Rewrites a pipeline producer when every downstream stage is an undecorated
+  display-only `head`, `tail`, or `cat` consumer.
+- Added Codex initialization through `AGENTS.md` + `RTK.md`, init dry-run mode,
+  and explicit custom-filter trust selection.
+- Wired trusted TOML filters into hook rewriting with reversible truncation and
+  recovery hints.
+
+### Changed
+- Search and Cargo JSON paths now stream output and preserve native diagnostics,
+  line-number shape, context separators, and signal exit status.
+- `git stash show` keeps its native default diffstat and compacts it; `git checkout`
+  now has a parity-preserving RTK route.
+- Pipeline final-stage rewriting is limited to output-transparent RTK search
+  filters; pipe-feeding stages remain raw unless all consumers are display-only.
+
+### Fixed
+- Prevented false-success summaries for failed pytest, mypy, and Ruff runs.
+- Made permission normalization, JSON extraction, analytics truncation, and tee
+  recovery paths safe for whitespace, UTF-8, and shell-special path characters.
+- Accepted the current ccusage `period` key and propagated signal-derived exit
+  codes through passthrough execution.
+
+## [0.43.0-fork.4] - 2026-07-28
+
+Exact-output safety for rewrite hooks and agent workflows.
+
+### Added
+- Added the visible `rtk raw <cmd>` alias for tracked, unfiltered proxy execution.
+- Added agent guidance for exact pipelines, generated files, checksums, counts,
+  parsing, and local or remote command output.
+
+### Fixed
+- Commands that redirect stdout to a file now bypass automatic RTK rewriting,
+  preventing summaries and `[N more lines]` markers from being persisted as data.
+- Preserved filtering for stderr-only redirects, fd duplication, and
+  stdout redirected to `/dev/null`.
+
+## [0.43.0-fork.3] - 2026-07-15
+
+Init and generated-instruction refresh on the stable upstream v0.43.0 base.
+
+### Changed
+- Replaced the duplicated shell rewrite engine with an upstream-style thin hook
+  delegating to `rtk rewrite`, while preserving the host's permission checks.
+- Reduced global `RTK.md` from 146 to 44 lines and project inline instructions
+  from about 200 to 52 lines; command discovery now uses `rtk --help`.
+- Registered only the Bash rewrite hook during global init. Obsolete native-tool
+  blockers are removed while unrelated and memory-layer hooks are preserved.
+- Documented engine-faithful `rtk rg` and `rtk grep`, automatic exact range reads,
+  never-worse behavior, and optional atomic `rtk write` usage.
+
+### Fixed
+- Removed stale `rg -> grep` guidance, hard-deny policies, unavailable macOS
+  `timeout` usage, fixed line-count claims, and the unconditional subagent block.
+
+## [0.43.0-fork.2] - 2026-07-15
+
+P0/P1 upstream parity wave on the current stable upstream v0.43.0 base.
+
+### Added
+- Native, engine-faithful `rtk grep` and `rtk rg` with stdin support, native flag
+  semantics, error propagation, bounded compression, and upstream integration suites.
+- OpenShift `oc` routing through shared Kubernetes filters.
+- Global never-worse output guard and recovery-hint accounting across direct filters.
+
+### Fixed
+- Propagated Git status, stash, worktree, and commit failures; made commit hash parsing
+  Unicode-safe.
+- Preserved binary curl responses, init symlinks, explicit Vitest reporters, `uv run`
+  rewrites, SIGPIPE behavior, and native command exit codes.
+
